From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?John=20T=C3=B6rnblom?= <john.tornblom@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 14:39:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ps4: the TV remote's options and disc menu keys

On the TV's remote over HDMI-CEC, options is reported as the controller's
TRIANGLE and disc menu as SQUARE, not as OPTIONS or a CEC key code, so
neither key gave anything. Options is now Menu, as OPTIONS already is, and
disc menu is F10, after guide's F9. OPTIONS stays Menu, for a remote that
reports it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EVpxQmphxjyzGFQPpgqSkT
---
 docs/README-ps4.md            |  1 +
 src/video/ps4/SDL_ps4remote.c | 13 ++++++++-----
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/README-ps4.md b/docs/README-ps4.md
index 999943c..d9a4696 100644
--- a/docs/README-ps4.md
+++ b/docs/README-ps4.md
@@ -103,6 +103,7 @@ Drivers
   | camera, display            | F3, F4                       |
   | red, green, yellow, blue   | F5, F6, F7, F8               |
   | guide                      | F9                           |
+  | disc menu                  | F10                          |
   | channel + / -              | PageUp, PageDown             |
   | previous channel           | Backspace                    |
 * Filesystem: `SDL_GetBasePath()` is the program's folder (from `argv[0]`,
diff --git a/src/video/ps4/SDL_ps4remote.c b/src/video/ps4/SDL_ps4remote.c
index 620067d..088bbc1 100644
--- a/src/video/ps4/SDL_ps4remote.c
+++ b/src/video/ps4/SDL_ps4remote.c
@@ -25,11 +25,12 @@
 /* A media remote, on libScePad's remote control port, as keys.
 
    This is the TV's remote over HDMI-CEC (with "Enable HDMI Device Link"
-   on), or a media remote. The arrows, X, O and OPTIONS are reported as
-   the controller's buttons; every other key is reported as a CEC key code
-   in the pad state, as on the PS5. The remote is not a joystick: it only
-   sends key events. When the port cannot be opened, there is simply no
-   remote. */
+   on), or a media remote. The arrows, OK, back, options and disc menu
+   are reported as the controller's buttons (options as TRIANGLE and disc
+   menu as SQUARE, on the TV's remote); every other key is reported as a
+   CEC key code in the pad state, as on the PS5. The remote is not a
+   joystick: it only sends key events. When the port cannot be opened,
+   there is simply no remote. */
 
 #include "SDL_events.h"
 #include "../../events/SDL_keyboard_c.h"
@@ -50,6 +51,8 @@ static const struct
     { PS4_PAD_BUTTON_CROSS, SDL_SCANCODE_RETURN },  /* "ok" */
     { PS4_PAD_BUTTON_CIRCLE, SDL_SCANCODE_ESCAPE }, /* "back" */
     { PS4_PAD_BUTTON_OPTIONS, SDL_SCANCODE_MENU },
+    { PS4_PAD_BUTTON_TRIANGLE, SDL_SCANCODE_MENU }, /* "options" */
+    { PS4_PAD_BUTTON_SQUARE, SDL_SCANCODE_F10 },    /* "disc menu" */
 };
 
 /* The CEC key code, indexed by its value; 0 is no key. */
-- 
